{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a table.</b> After the making of the ark, which was like a throne for the Shekhinah, as it says: <b>and I will meet with you there</b>, He commanded concerning the table and the menorah according to the custom before princes, as in the matter of the Shunammite in her saying: וְנָשִׂים לוֹ שָׁם מִטָּה וְשֻׁלְחָן וְכִסֵּא וּמְנוֹרָה (2 Kings 4:10). And the crown of the table signifies the crown of kingship, as the Sages of blessed memory said. Now the king's governance of the state is twofold: the first in matters of judgment and other arrangements of the state; the second, to defend the state against every foe and enemy, as it says: וּשְׁפָטָנוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ... וְנִלְחַם אֶת מִלְחֲמֹתֵינוּ (1 Samuel 8:20). Therefore two crowns were placed on the table: one for the table itself, signifying the provisioning of the state and the ordering of its affairs; and the second for the frame (מִסְגֶּרֶת), signifying that it shields her from all harm and puts an end to the enemy and the avenger."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:16.175274831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}